  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "Thanks, Sam. You're verified, and I've checked order Q-8001 from Burger Barn.\n\nThe courier's log shows this:\n- The courier picked up the order at 6:47 PM and arrived at your address at 7:05 PM.\n- The courier called you at 7:06 PM and 7:09 PM and got no answer.\n- At 7:15 PM the delivery was marked failed because the courier couldn't reach you.\n- The order went back to the restaurant at 7:28 PM.\n\nOur policy doesn't allow a refund or credit when a delivery fails because the customer couldn't be reached. That means I can't refund or credit this order. I'm sorry, I know that's frustrating.\n\nIf you think the courier had the wrong contact details or went to the wrong place, tell me and I'll note it. I can also pass this to a specialist if you'd like to speak with someone."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Wait, the order number is 8001, not Q-8001. Anyway, so I just lose my money? I was in the shower when they came, so my phone was on silent. I only saw the missed calls later."
  },
  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "I understand, Sam, and I'm sorry. Order 8001 and Q-8001 are the same order in our system. It's the Burger Barn order placed at 6:20 PM today for $28.03.\n\nI still can't refund or credit it. The courier arrived on time, called you twice, and waited about 10 minutes before the delivery was marked failed. Our policy doesn't cover failed deliveries where the customer couldn't be reached, even when the reason was an honest mix-up like this one. I can't make an exception.\n\nIf you'd like to talk to a person about it, I can pass your case to a specialist. They'd follow up within 24 hours. I can't promise what they'd decide. Would you like me to do that?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Ugh, fine. I'd rather not wait another day for an answer that's probably the same, though. Okay, I'll take it. Thanks for checking."
  }
